<%#
  Get USDC — the TEACHING half of the funds wall, and the single answer the
  entry blocker now gives whichever funding method came up short.

  WHY IT REPLACED A SPLIT. showFundsNeeded used to branch on session.mode alone:
  web2 to Buy an Entry Token, web3 to Top Up Wallet. That fork asked the wrong
  question. What a blocked player lacks is money for this entry, and the mode
  they signed in under does not change the answer — it only changed which modal
  they were shown. In production it changed it to a modal with no visible rails
  at all (ENABLE_COINFLOW unset, PAYMENT_PROVIDER none, STRIPE_CHECKOUT_DISABLED
  true), so the wall read "pick how to pay" over an empty box while the USDC rail
  it never offered was the only funded path on the chain. One answer, both cases.

  BUILT FROM ENGINE BLOCKS, deliberately (operator call, 2026-09-05). The modal
  this one is modelled on, modals/_wallet_setup, hand-rolls its close mark and
  its wallet row even though studio/modals/blocks ships both; the shapes drifted
  because nothing made them share. This composes blocks/_close_x and
  blocks/_rail_row so a change to the house idiom reaches it for free.

  ONE ROUTE: BUY USDC INSIDE PHANTOM. The CDP/Coinbase onramp has no legal
  clearance (operator, 2026-09-06), so this card must not offer it — a revision
  that led with it has been removed. Signup mints no custodial wallet
  (AppFlags.web3_only_onboarding? defaults ON), so a new account links Phantom
  and funds the entry from there; the managed wallets that predate that flag are
  legacy, and this card has nothing to sell them (see the limitation below).

  THIS IS THE FUNDS-NEEDED VALIDATION NOTICE. showFundsNeeded routes here when a
  player tries to enter without USDC and without an entry token — it is the card
  that says what is missing and how to get it, not a payment surface.

  THE BAND ALWAYS SHIPS A PLAYER. buy_usdc_video? cannot return false: the id
  falls back to BuyUsdcHelper::DEFAULT_VIDEO_ID, so BUY_USDC_VIDEO_ID only swaps
  WHICH video plays, never whether one does. The guard below is the seam that
  keeps that decision in the helper, not an optional-band switch.

  CRITICAL: rendered inside the host template x-if, so a SINGLE root element.
  x-data is a double-quoted attribute, so single-quote everything inside the
  Alpine expressions.
%>
<div x-data="{
       videoMuted: true,
       get props() { return ($store.modals.current() || {}).props || {} },
       unmuteVideo: function() {
         this.videoMuted = false
         try {
           var frame = this.$refs.videoFrame
           if (frame && frame.contentWindow) {
             frame.contentWindow.postMessage('{\'event\':\'command\',\'func\':\'unMute\',\'args\':[]}', '*')
           }
         } catch (e) {}
       }
     }"
     class="relative">

  <%# Engine close mark. The parent is class="relative" above, which this
      absolutely-positioned button anchors to. %>
  <%= render "studio/modals/blocks/close_x" %>

  <%# The card's image: the USDC disc badged with Solana. It names the asset at
      a glance, and it is the only place this card states the CHAIN — the copy
      below names USDC and digital dollars and never says Solana, so the badge
      carries that half alone. See blocks/_usdc_solana_mark. %>
  <div class="flex justify-center pt-2 mb-3">
    <%= render "modals/blocks/usdc_solana_mark", size: 64 %>
  </div>

  <div class="text-center mb-2">
    <h3 class="text-heading font-bold text-lg leading-tight">Get USDC</h3>
  </div>
  <p class="text-xs text-body mb-4 text-center">
    To enter the contest you will need to fund your wallet with USDC, which is a
    form of digital dollars.
  </p>

  <%# THE PHANTOM ROW (operator call, 2026-09-05 — replaced a Coinbase rail_row).
      A player at this wall already has a wallet; buying inside Phantom is one
      screen away for them, where the Coinbase hand-off was three.

      IT IS NOT blocks/_rail_row, and that is a known cost rather than an
      oversight. The primitive draws its icon as a letter or an emoji in a tinted
      tile — there is no slot for a brand <svg><use>, nor for the ml-auto action
      label this idiom puts opposite the name. So this is the SECOND hand-rolled
      copy of the house wallet row (modals/_wallet_setup has the first, and
      solana-studio's _wallet_connect a third inline). Promoting it to an engine
      primitive is a studio-engine change and is tracked separately; until then
      the markup here is copied from _wallet_setup's mobile row verbatim so the
      two at least stay identical.

      A REAL LINK, not a button: it navigates off-site, and the rail_row contract
      says outright that a rail which must navigate should be a plain anchor. %>
  <%# Brand sprite. MUST live inside this single root — a sibling would be
      dropped by the host's template x-if, painting an empty icon. %>
  <%= render "studio/modals/blocks/wallet_brand_sprite" %>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%# THE ONE ROUTE, because it is the only one this app is cleared to offer.
        The CDP/Coinbase onramp has NO LEGAL CLEARANCE (operator, 2026-09-06),
        which is what its numbers were quietly saying all along: 27 attempts in
        prod, 26 expired, 1 success, nothing since 2026-06-29. A revision of this
        card led with that rail; leading a funds wall with an uncleared payment
        path is worse than any layout mistake, so it is gone.

        Phantom is not a fallback here — it IS the funding path. Signup mints no
        custodial wallet (AppFlags.web3_only_onboarding? defaults ON), so every
        new account links Phantom and buys USDC inside it.

        Not blocks/_rail_row: that primitive draws its icon as a letter or emoji
        in a tinted tile and has no slot for a brand <svg><use> or the ml-auto
        action label this idiom puts opposite the name. Markup copied verbatim
        from _wallet_setup's mobile row so the two stay identical until an engine
        wallet-row primitive exists. %>
    <a href="<%= phantom_buy_url %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
       class="w-full flex items-center gap-3 p-3 rounded-xl bg-surface-alt border border-strong hover:bg-surface transition text-left no-underline"
       data-usdc-rail="phantom">
      <svg class="w-9 h-9" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#se-wallet-phantom"></use></svg>
      <span class="font-semibold text-heading">Phantom</span>
      <span class="ml-auto flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-xs text-muted uppercase tracking-wide">Open Phantom</span>
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" class="w-4 h-4 text-muted">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m8.25 4.5 7.5 7.5-7.5 7.5" />
        </svg>
      </span>
    </a>
  </div>

  <%# === NEW TO USDC =========================================================
      The teaching half, same shape as the wallet card's "New to Solana" band:
      someone walking it on screen, playing HERE, because a half-finished entry
      should not have to leave the page to find out what a stablecoin is.

      Muted autoplay is the only autoplay a browser permits on a modal that
      opened without a click, and the overlay turns the glance it earns into a
      choice. youtube-nocookie, so a player nobody pressed sets no cookie. %>
  <div class="mt-5 pt-4 border-t border-strong">
    <h4 class="text-heading font-semibold text-sm mb-1.5">New to USDC &#129300;</h4>
    <p class="text-xs text-body mb-3">
      How to buy USDC inside your wallet, in <strong class="font-semibold text-heading">two minutes</strong>.
    </p>

    <% if buy_usdc_video? %>
      <div class="relative w-full aspect-video rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-strong bg-black">
        <iframe src="<%= buy_usdc_video_embed_url %>"
                x-ref="videoFrame"
                title="How to buy USDC"
                class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full"
                allow="autoplay; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture; fullscreen"
                referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
                allowfullscreen></iframe>

        <%# Covers the whole player on purpose: while the video is silent every
            click should mean the same thing, and a click landing on the player
            would pause it instead. It leaves for good on that click. %>
        <button type="button" x-show="videoMuted" @click="unmuteVideo()"
                class="group absolute inset-0 w-full h-full flex items-center justify-center bg-black/20 hover:bg-black/10 transition border-0 cursor-pointer"
                aria-label="Unmute the video">
          <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full bg-black/75 px-3 py-1.5 text-[11px] font-semibold text-white shadow-lg transition group-hover:bg-black/90">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" class="w-3.5 h-3.5">
              <path d="M13 4.2a.8.8 0 0 0-1.32-.6L7.4 7.3H4.6A1.6 1.6 0 0 0 3 8.9v6.2a1.6 1.6 0 0 0 1.6 1.6h2.8l4.28 3.7a.8.8 0 0 0 1.32-.6V4.2Z" />
              <path d="M16.4 8.6a.9.9 0 0 1 1.27 0L19.5 10.4l1.83-1.83a.9.9 0 1 1 1.27 1.27L20.77 11.7l1.83 1.83a.9.9 0 1 1-1.27 1.27L19.5 13l-1.83 1.83a.9.9 0 0 1-1.27-1.27l1.83-1.83-1.83-1.83a.9.9 0 0 1 0-1.27Z" />
            </svg>
            Tap for sound
          </span>
        </button>
      </div>

      <p class="text-[11px] text-muted mt-1.5 text-center">
        <a href="<%= buy_usdc_video_watch_url %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
           class="underline hover:text-secondary">Watch on YouTube</a>
      </p>
    <% end %>

    <%# The read-it-instead route. Neutral tone: it is a real control, and it
        must not out-shout the Buy USDC rail above, which is the ask. %>
    <% guide_url = buy_usdc_guide_url %>
    <% guide_target = buy_usdc_guide_external? ? "_blank" : nil %>
    <% guide_rel = buy_usdc_guide_external? ? "noopener noreferrer" : nil %>
    <a href="<%= guide_url %>" target="<%= guide_target %>" rel="<%= guide_rel %>"
       class="btn btn-neutral w-full mt-3 gap-2 no-underline" data-usdc-guide>
      Detailed Guide
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" class="w-4 h-4">
        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m8.25 4.5 7.5 7.5-7.5 7.5" />
      </svg>
    </a>
  </div>

  <%# NO "MORE WAYS TO ADD FUNDS" LINK, and its absence is deliberate.
      modals/_wallet_topup leads with the CDP/Coinbase rail and modals/_onramp_hub
      offers it again; neither is legally cleared, so routing a blocked player
      there from the funds wall would hand them the one path this app must not
      sell. An orphaned showWalletTopup is a code-health cost; sending users to an
      uncleared payment rail is a compliance one, and they are not comparable.

      That leaves showWalletTopup with no caller from this wall — a REAL loose end
      that review previously (and correctly) flagged. It is not resolvable inside
      this card: what to do with Top Up Wallet and the Add Funds hub while the
      onramp is uncleared is an operator decision about those two surfaces, not a
      modal fix. Escalated rather than papered over. %>
  <button type="button" @click="$store.modals.close()"
          class="mt-2 w-full text-center text-sm text-secondary hover:text-heading">
    Maybe later
  </button>
</div>
